Third-party notices: @stencil/react-output-target (MIT)
================================================================================

Reviewed upstream release: 1.8.1.

@kimen/react is generated by Stencil's React output target, and each wrapper
calls the target's runtime (createComponent, over @lit/react). The package
build copies that runtime, unchanged, from the installed output target into
dist/stencil-runtime: its modules (runtime.js and its create-component
chunk), their source maps, which carry the runtime's original source, and
its declarations. The wrappers import the copy, so a consumer installs
neither the output target nor its build-time dependencies.

